<article class="env-remark" id="0ESX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ESX">Remark <span data-tag="0ESX">42.45.1</span>.</a> In the discussion above we have defined the components of the Chern character $ch_ p(\mathcal{E}) \in A^ p(X) \otimes \mathbf{Q}$ of $\mathcal{E}$ even if the rank of $\mathcal{E}$ is not constant. See Remarks <a href="/tag/0ESW" data-tag="0ESW">42.38.10</a> and <a href="/tag/0FA7" data-tag="0FA7">42.43.5</a>. Thus the full Chern character of $\mathcal{E}$ is an element of $\prod _{p \geq 0} (A^ p(X) \otimes \mathbf{Q})$. If $X$ is quasi-compact and $\dim (X) < \infty $ (usual dimension), then one can show using Lemma <a href="/tag/0FDX" data-tag="0FDX">42.34.6</a> and the splitting principle that $ch(\mathcal{E}) \in A^*(X) \otimes \mathbf{Q}$. </p>
</article>